  "lineage": "Recreational music and dance created by Ga youth in the Bukom area of central Accra in the early 1960s and credited to Otoo Lincoln, drawing on older Ga rhythms and on highlife and rock and roll dancing. Groups of peg-tuned kpanlogo drums play under call-and-response songs with a bell, rattles and handclaps; generic cards stand in for the bell and rattle.",
